# Copy this file to .env in this folder and fill it in, or run pnpm configure at the repository root, which
# asks and writes it (mode 600). .env is git-ignored; never commit a real key. The server reads it when
# ENV_FILE=<path> names it (pnpm start does that). Nothing here is needed to run the tests.
# Every other setting, with its default, is in the guide's section 14.12 and in apps/clinic/.env.example.

# The conversation's model (agent.yaml's model.default, Muse Ember on Meta's API): its key.
# META_API_KEY=

# The decision model, which reads a caller's yes to a read-back: with JEV_CLIENT=jev and its key. Under the
# stub no yes is read, so nothing is ever booked or sent.
# JEV_CLIENT=jev
# TYPESAFE_API_KEY=

# The phone line. pnpm start sets PUBLIC_HOST itself when it is unset (a quick tunnel). The carriers the line
# answers, a comma list: twilio, telnyx, or both; none for the web chat alone (CHAT=on). A carrier's secret is
# needed only when it is listed. An agent app's calls are interruptible by speech and, on Telnyx, have the
# playback events on, whatever BARGE_IN and TELNYX_EVENTS say; their voice on each carrier is agent.yaml's
# persona.voices (its Twilio voice is Google's: TTS_PROVIDER=Google, set with TTS_VOICE, speaks it).
# PUBLIC_HOST=
# VOICE_PROVIDERS=twilio
# TWILIO_AUTH_TOKEN=
# TELNYX_PUBLIC_KEY=
# TTS_PROVIDER=Google
# TTS_VOICE=en-US-Neural2-F

# agent.yaml names no transfer number (there is no live transfer: a caller who asks for a person leaves a
# callback note). HANDOFF_NUMBER is where a call the server cannot keep goes (a restart with no store, a
# reconnect given up): the shop's own phone. A 555 number is fine for local use.
# HANDOFF_NUMBER=+15555550100

# The shop's phone, which gets a text summary of every request, booking and callback note (src/shopTexts.ts),
# and the number texts are sent from, with the Twilio account (guide 13.17). Unset, texts are printed, not sent.
# SHOP_PHONE=+15555550101
# TEXT_FROM=+15555550102
# TWILIO_ACCOUNT_SID=
# TEXT_LIMIT_EXEMPT=+15555550101

# A tester's own phone, recognised as the demo dealership (agent.yaml's env.DEALER_TEST_LINE). Set it privately
# here, never in agent.yaml; unset, it is left out.
# DEALER_TEST_LINE=+15555550103

# Where the shop page's log is kept (src/shopLog.ts); unset, in memory alone.
# SHOP_DATA_DIR=

# A Google calendar (agent.yaml's sources.calendar with kind: google and calendarId, guide 14.12): the
# service account's JSON key file, kept outside the repository (a placeholder path below). Read only where
# agent.yaml's calendar is google and the code makes it (businessCalendar); the shop's code keeps its own
# stand-in calendar (src/shop.ts) for now. To block a day on the Google calendar, put in an all-day event and
# set it to show as busy: Google shows an all-day event as free unless told otherwise, and one shown as free
# takes no place. The calendar's time limit (4 s) is per request to Google, and one booking may make four (a
# sign-in, the day's listing, the insert, and a read of the event where the insert went unanswered).
# GOOGLE_CALENDAR_KEY_FILE=/path/outside/the/repository/service-account-key.json

# BRIDGE_AFTER_MS: on a call, how long a turn waits for its reply's first words before the bridge ("One sec."),
# 0 to 10000 ms, default 2500 (guide 14.12).
# BRIDGE_AFTER_MS=2500
